let's get reaction to all of this news  involving Russia the latest on the  investigation also surrounding Russia  here in the u.s. from Senate Judiciary  Committee Chairman Chuck Grassley and  committee member Senator Lindsey Graham  I sat down with them this afternoon  in the Judiciary Committee hearing room  on Capitol Hill and started by asking  about the administration's new sanctions  against Russia well I'm glad to know  that it's happening and secondly because  of the 2016 2016 election very good  reason for doing it but there's plenty  of reasons for doing it otherwise all  you got to think about is Ukraine and  their interference and the Baltics  Georgia and Crimea in all that they're  trying to recreate a Soviet state and we  got to put a stop to it I can't say much  better as 98 to 2 vote by the Senate we  can't agree on much of anything in the  Senate but 98 senators voted for these  sanctions and up until today really they  had not been implemented by the  administration clearly the assassination  in Great Britain had an effect here this  was a nerve agent associated with the  Russian military clearly Russia was  involved here so I'm very pleased but we  need to do more you on the committee  have released a series of letters today  calling for a special Council another  special council why I would like to  suggest to you that you use the word  special consul yes because of what it is  but we're thinking in terms of a special  council to work with the inspector  general we have all kinds of confidence  in the Inspector General's work we know  he's a good person we know he's doing  good work digs in deep he's got a staff  of maybe about 400 but he doesn't have  the capability of working with people  that have left the Justice Department he  can only bring in those people that are  already in government to investigate and  this special consul working in a team  and I want to emphasize the word team  with the Inspector General we'll give  him the tools he needs to get all the  information that we're asking to get and  we sent him 30 questions that we  want investigators I mean there's a lot  of questions in here I mean are you  seeing things that are really red flags  for you that you've seen that that are  not getting answered number one chairman  Grassley has done a very good job of  looking at all things Russia we've had  hearings in our committee about how  Russia operates we've brought in Sally  Yates and and clapper and a bunch of  other people who are worried about the  Trump campaign association with the  Russians we haven't found any evidence  collusion but Muller is doing his job  the Chairman and I have looked real  close at the FBI investigation of the  Clinton email scandal and I've come way  believing that it was shockingly done  that there were conflicts of interest  that there was political bias that may  have resulted in giving Clinton to pass  the steel dossier was paid for by the  Democratic Party diffusion GPS mr.  Steele had associates in Russia that  could have easily compromised him and we  believe the FISA warrant process was  abused and the reason we want a special  counsel is I think crimes may have been  committed mr. Steele was sued in May of  2017 in Great Britain for libel somebody  mentioned in the dossier sued him in  British Court and in the response to the  lawsuit he admitted in British Court  that he had talked to media outlets in  September of 2016  about the dossier the FBI told the FISA  Court all through 2016  September October in November that mr.  Steele had no contacts at all with the  media when it comes to shopping around  the dossier so we have a filing in  British Court where a lawyer from mr.  Steele admits to talking to the American  media worldwide media in September at  the same time of 2016 the FBI was using  him as a confidential informant somebody  needs to look and see whether or not who  he's lying to we'll give him the tools  to do it because they cannot be counted  on to investigate themselves I mean it's  kind of common sense if you do something  wrong you don't have  Fox garden the chicken house so what are  we investigating here the number four  person Department of Justice Bruce ORS  wife worked for fusion GPS he had dozens  of contacts with mr. steel the informant  the FBI was using on the payroll of the  Democratic Party there's no way in the  world he should have interactive with  mr. steel cause his wife worked for the  same organization so somebody other than  the people in charge today needs to look  at what they did yesterday do you think  Andrew McCabe should be fired before he  retires  I don't not sure I want to make that  judgment right now I think it could  happen but I know I have great respect  for OPR the Office of Professional  Responsibility and they have found  something grossly wrong but I'm not  going to draw a line on what should be  done about it  something could it could happen but you  know we've raised enough questions about  him over a long period of time and I  suggested to certain people they oughta  been fired  just soon as we got a new Attorney  General well the the punishment for  violating the law should be you lose  your job if the in fact did authorize  FBI agents to talk to the media and lied  about and seeing what you've seen you  think you did well I don't know we'll  leave that up here's what I do know that  the FBI and the Department of Justice  were corrupt in my view when it came to  handling the email investigation of  Clinton and the entire FISA warrant  application process was abused and one  last thing  not one Democrat seems to care about  this why did we start out with this the  Trump Russia was the start of it but you  follow the facts and the facts led us to  that there's a lot of things done in the  previous administration so today I was  criticized in my committee by Democrats  that why are we interested in in the  previous administration well if there's  political interference in the Justice  Department the FBI in one administration  and that's what we were looking into  wouldn't it be natural that it's wrong  in the previous administration the  president said today that stories about  a major shake-up in his administration  are wrong  are overwritten but clearly he's  considering some additional changes  including what has already happened with  Rex Tillerson if he did fire jeff  Sessions how would that go over in the  Judiciary Committee I would only answer  your question this way unless you push  me on it I don't think he should be  fired I'll push you on it what do you  think would happen they'd blow up the  committee the chairman has done a  wonderful job getting nominees out of  the committee with a lot of obstruction  but if you had to replace the Attorney  General Jeff Sessions was somebody knew  it would blow the place up it'd be seen  as an effort to undermine the momentum  investigation it locked the Senate down  and I need Jeff Sessions done a good job  have you've heard Lance have you read  plans to do that I have people in  journalism like you asking us that and I  gave the same answer to you but remember  this administration's got enough to do  there's a hundred vacancies in the court  now that my committee has to deal with  well we don't have time to deal with a  lot of things that are going fairly  smoothly but one last thing about what  brought us here today if the shoe were  on the other foot can you imagine how  the media would be reacting that if you  found that the lead investigator of an  investigation had a political bias  against Clinton and for Trump that if  there was a dossier used by the FBI to  get a FISA warrant and the Republican  Party paid a foreign agent go to Russia  to get information on Hillary Clinton  how they would be behaving today all I  can say to my Democratic colleagues I  have supported Muller having the  independence to do this job but if you  don't think it's wrong for the FBI to  use a paid political informant and  present court a dossier that's been  unverified then I disagree so the bottom  line here folks is that what the FBI and  the DOJ did in terms of investigating  Clinton and the initial investigation  regarding the Trump campaign really  bothers me and I want somebody other  than a politician looking at it chances  that you get a special counsel in  addition to what's already there  we'll be shocked if somebody doesn't see  the inherent conflict in the Department  of Justice regarding investigating  itself high probability I'm going to use  as much leverage as I can and I think I  have a lot to get the job done  senators we appreciate the time thank  you okay thanks

